AGEP: Age (Numeric)
COW: Class of worker (Categorical)
SCHL: Educational attainment (Categorical)
MAR: Marital status (Categorical)
OCCP: Occupation recode for 2018 and later based on 2018 OCC codes (Categorical)
POBP: Place of birth (Recode) (Categorical?)
RELP: Relationship (Categorical)
WKHP: Usual hours worked per week past 12 months (Numeric)
SEX: Sex (Categorical)
RAC1P: Recoded detailed race code (Categorical)
PINCP: Total person's income (boolean label: income > 50000)

POBP: us_region_code (Bureau of Economic Analysis regions):
NW = New England (Connecticut, Maine, Massachusetts, New Hampshire, Rhode Island, and Vermont)
MD = Mideast (Delaware, Maryland, New Jersey, New York, Pennsylvania, and Washington, D.C)
GL = Great Lakes (Illinois, Indiana, Michigan, Ohio, and Wisconsin)
PN = Plains (Iowa, Kansas, Minnesota, Missouri, Nebraska, North Dakota, and South Dakota)
SE = Southeast (Alabama, Arkansas, Florida, Georgia, Kentucky, Louisiana, Mississippi, North Carolina, South Carolina, Tennessee, Virginia, and West Virginia)
SW = Southwest (Arizona, New Mexico, Oklahoma, and Texas)
RM = Rocky Mountain (Colorado, Idaho, Montana, Utah, and Wyoming)
FW = Far West (Alaska, California, Hawaii, Nevada, Oregon, and Washington)

POBP: World area of birth:
PI = PR and US Island Areas (POBP = 061-099)
LA = Latin America (POBP = 303,310-399)
AS = Asia (POBP = 158-159,161,200-299)
EU = Europe (POBP = 100-157,160,162-199)
AF = Africa (POBP = 400-499)
NA = Northern America (POBP = 300-302,304-309)
OS = Oceania and at Sea (POBP = 060,500-554)